WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:28.933
I almost got married once.

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:45.233
Wentworth held my heart.

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:02.067
But he was a sailor

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:04.567
without rank or fortune.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.867
And I was persuaded
to give him up.

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:25.267
Now I'm single and thriving.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.433
I spend my time
drinking fine wines,

00:01:29.967 --> 00:01:32.100
enjoying warm baths…

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.667
and lying face down
on my bed.

00:01:39.433 --> 00:01:41.433
Like I said, thriving.

00:01:43.833 --> 00:01:46.100
Who needs romance
when one has…

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.233
family?

00:02:05.833 --> 00:02:06.900
My father.

00:02:07.833 --> 00:02:10.667
He's never met a reflective
surface he didn't like.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.733
Vanity is the beginning
and end of his character.

00:02:15.933 --> 00:02:16.900
Also the middle.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.733
"Sir Walter Elliot,

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.200
born March 1st, 1760."

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:22.700
"Man of consequence,

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:25.400
known for his
exquisite jawline."

00:02:28.633 --> 00:02:30.000
He is the sole object

00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:33.267
of his own warmest respect
and devotion.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.767
One's family is only
escapable by two things:

00:02:39.333 --> 00:02:41.367
marriage and death.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.800
Both seem unlikely
in the immediate future.

00:02:46.233 --> 00:02:48.800
"Married July 15th, 1784,
to Jane."

00:02:49.233 --> 00:02:50.233
My mother.

00:02:52.533 --> 00:02:55.000
-I miss her.
-"Jane died in 1801."

00:02:55.067 --> 00:02:58.267
"By her, Sir Walter issued
three children."

00:02:58.700 --> 00:02:59.800
My sisters.

00:03:00.333 --> 00:03:02.633
"Elizabeth,
celebrated beauty

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:06.067
and Somerset's most
fashion-forward luminary."

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:09.233
Elizabeth, the eldest.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:11.533
"Mary, married
to Charles Musgrove,

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.967
heir to the superior
Uppercross estate."

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:16.767
Mary, the youngest.

00:03:16.833 --> 00:03:19.867
"And Anne,
born August 9th, 1787."

00:03:24.867 --> 00:03:27.200
And me, middle child,

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.667
the crack
in his looking glass.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:31.833
Shame there wasn't
anything nice

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.833
we could think to add
about you, Anne.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:35.667
Thanks for trying.

00:03:35.733 --> 00:03:36.700
You're quite welcome.

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:38.233
I wanted to leave
you out entirely,

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.167
but Daddy thought people
might think you had died.

00:03:43.533 --> 00:03:45.033
-Debt collectors.
-Daddy.

00:03:45.567 --> 00:03:46.433
Daddy!

00:03:47.867 --> 00:03:50.267
The one thing my father
loves more than himself

00:03:50.333 --> 00:03:51.600
is spending money.

00:03:51.667 --> 00:03:53.967
It was always going
to run out one day.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:57.033
-Daddy…
-Daddy's broke, princess.

00:03:57.467 --> 00:03:58.700
Playtime's over.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:07.567
There, there.

